  "limitations": [
    "A missing or outdated remote rule provider may still leave unclassified traffic to later rules. Native AI fallbacks cover recognized brands, not every future domain. This is not a universal fail-closed gate.",
    "Type partitioning removes duplicated early/late exact-domain matching; independent remote sources still do not update as a transaction.",
    "Shared Google/YouTube IPs cannot uniquely identify YouTube without a recognizable domain.",
    "The complete requested AI source includes shared infrastructure. Its classification scope does not imply AI-exclusive ownership.",
    "Manual DIRECT is intentionally available in scene groups. DNS, TUN, IPv6 and browser WebRTC behavior remain client-controlled.",
    "Tests use public fixtures and loopback mocks; they do not validate real logins, region unlock, playback, public exits, system TUN or comprehensive WebRTC protection."
  ],
